<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>World leaders gather at UN amid wars, AI fears and global divisions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5260d2a9570b57c2dfc92a1a5b65367495bb6db285ee784faf54943da3833b0</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T03:49:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-world-leaders-gather-at-un-amid-wars-ai-fears-and-global-divisions--d1ee36515d6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-world-leaders-gather-at-un-amid-wars-ai-fears-and-global-divisions" /><summary type="html">World leaders are gathering at the United Nations this week against a backdrop of wars in the Middle East and Ukraine, rising fears over artificial intelligence and mounting economic and climate pressures. The annual General Assembly will test whether the 193-member body can still bring countries together to tackle crises that increasingly transcend borders.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Yemen fighting escalates as Trump heads to UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29f691ac006b78f4015249af5c83e57827eda6066f67a64fda955fcf1ce02cc2</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T03:41:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260922-middle-east-live-yemen-fighting-escalates-as-trump-heads-to-un--4465411a8b3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260922-middle-east-live-yemen-fighting-escalates-as-trump-heads-to-un" /><summary type="html">Saudi airstrikes on Yemen's Red Sea port of Mokha have killed at least six people as Iran-backed Houthis press their offensive. The escalation comes as the US and its allies face growing pressure to protect Saudi Arabia and regional energy infrastructure, while Donald Trump prepares to address the UN in New York. Follow our live blog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UK and US make first-ever torpedo test from uncrewed vessel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5f52b9fce03978b34efa0e30dd051325141f57efdc2406197fe2f8720096677</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T02:33:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-uk-and-us-make-first-ever-torpedo-test-from-uncrewed-vessel--57411a117a8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-uk-and-us-make-first-ever-torpedo-test-from-uncrewed-vessel" /><summary type="html">The United Kingdom and the United States have for the first time test-fired a torpedo from an uncrewed underwater vessel, marking a step forward in AUKUS efforts to develop autonomous naval technology.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU fails to agree on lifting sanctions on Russian oligarchs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4be0a3b45b1cf92327253304db357d5351831221368502ed59f0a2ce63180574</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T02:18:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-eu-fails-to-agree-on-lifting-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs--e6657fec7a6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-eu-fails-to-agree-on-lifting-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs" /><summary type="html">EU countries failed Monday to reach a final deal that would remove Russian billionaires Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman from the bloc's sanctions list, with diplomats set to resume talks Tuesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US, Denmark and Greenland to sign security deal on Tuesday</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2550a98566588754f45618a47117f1e9467b1d1f04faf02321e26599f973cd87</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:10:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T23:30:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-denmark-and-greenland-to-sign-security-deal-on-tuesday--e3730ada4f03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-denmark-and-greenland-to-sign-security-deal-on-tuesday" /><summary type="html">The United States, Denmark and Greenland are set to sign a security agreement Tuesday expanding US involvement in Greenland’s defense while affirming Danish sovereignty over the Arctic territory.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount settles with US states to clear Warner Bros. mega-merger</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f622b0b672aaaec56d55074fd77b9ee28420de13decdc225c0849ac0e767a92</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T23:07:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-paramount-settles-with-us-states-to-clear-warner-bros-mega-merger--4bdfbeefe83c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-paramount-settles-with-us-states-to-clear-warner-bros-mega-merger" /><summary type="html">Paramount has reached a settlement with a group of US states that clears the way for its takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery, officials announced Monday, creating a Hollywood empire spanning television, news and cinema.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paramount settles with US states, clearing path for Warner Bros. merger</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d7cba2018937d4cb787eb686c3bfc4b36e91a1e0e80e3614ddf97472a23aafa0</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T22:48:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-paramount-settles-with-us-states-clearing-path-for-warner-bros-merger--f9c2a041c5b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-paramount-settles-with-us-states-clearing-path-for-warner-bros-merger" /><summary type="html">Paramount has reached a settlement with California and 11 other states that clears a major legal hurdle to its $110 billion takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery, with the deal imposing commitments on film production, jobs and editorial independence at CNN and CBS News.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's main armed groups form anti-government alliance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99dfd15cc4efb481c505e136a5ddc4be45154292d5c161fff36ac7fb1381204f</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T21:16:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-s-main-armed-groups-form-anti-government-alliance--d7f1443afa0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-s-main-armed-groups-form-anti-government-alliance" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, a coalition of opposition groups band together in the hope of ousting Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed. Also, I speak to the deputy chief of the UN's peacekeeping mission in DR Congo. And with just a few days to go before the legislative elections, young Moroccans are torn between hope and skepticism ahead of the crucial vote.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount, US states settle antitrust lawsuit over Warner Bros. acquisition</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:866929dee746c02c06bb8a831fb16ec495dbbb28070663e71e0d7f9a2bc823d0</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T21:13:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260921-paramount-us-states-settle-antitrust-lawsuit-over-warner-bros-acquisition--3e87e5401ca3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260921-paramount-us-states-settle-antitrust-lawsuit-over-warner-bros-acquisition" /><summary type="html">Paramount Skydance has settled a lawsuit with a dozen US states that sought to block its acquisition of Warner Brothers, as well as with the Writers Guild of America. California's Attorney General said that while the settlement addressed concerns over competition and protection, it did not mean a vote of support for the deal.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran hit by viral false claims after Macklemore controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cde07cdc1bc74afa6e9b5920d9b067b49fb0e9768bd1ac16e448e1469bbce1c</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T21:05:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-hit-by-viral-false-claims-after-macklemore-controversy-1--cd1d21c7e597.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-hit-by-viral-false-claims-after-macklemore-controversy-1" /><summary type="html">Ed Sheeran’s controversial US tour has sparked a wave of viral rumours. A false claim that his music was removed from Spotify racked up more than 3 million views on X, despite his his music remaining available. Another video, viewed over 14 million times, falsely suggested Sheeran was now defiantly performing solo after all his support acts withdrew, but not only is the footage dated, but Sheeran has indeed replaced the backing musicians. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Forbidden Stories on Trump deportation system: FRANCE 24's 'Ice, Trump and Africa'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb1054c32c2965ac3b4783c24eb2c7732d0f10190414dccc4a4412cd7f54e42b</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T19:52:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-forbidden-stories-on-trump-deportation-system-france24-s-ice-trump-and-africa--900722cdc76e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-forbidden-stories-on-trump-deportation-system-france24-s-ice-trump-and-africa" /><summary type="html">Sofia Alvarez Jurado, investigative journalist, member of the Deportation project speaks about the international investigation into Trump’s migrant policy.</summary></entry><entry><title>Infantino says open to FIFA reform talks after World Cup controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51c71e57fc7510c216312f7d5dc9d7e57f49767ecf8fe915a968193727e9660d</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T19:47:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260921-infantino-says-open-to-fifa-reform-talks-after-world-cup-controversy--e71402e87452.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260921-infantino-says-open-to-fifa-reform-talks-after-world-cup-controversy" /><summary type="html">FIFA ⁠President Gianni Infantino on Monday proposed an external review of how the football association makes decisions, including who has a say in major initiatives. Infantino ​faced backlash and calls for a boycott over the summer after proposing to sell a stake in the World Cup to private investors.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>France's new coach Zinedine Zidane leads first training session</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63e56735a083b92febaba1069dc38bc6e6d274bfced2f328f6a2c4cb0b1bb591</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T19:25:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260921-new-france-coach-zidane-leads-training-session-ahead-of-nations-league-campaign--8fd4cf153ea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260921-new-france-coach-zidane-leads-training-session-ahead-of-nations-league-campaign" /><summary type="html">France coach Zinedine Zidane on Monday oversaw his first training session with Les Bleus ahead of the new Nations League campaign. The 1998 World Cup winner led a dozen of his players through a light training session under the gaze of some 50 journalists.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>'Banking on a national brand': Bolsonaro sons Carlos, Jair Renan run for power in Brazil's south</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:186102126026e4aa45ad998710b60c87bdd9c4164fe7fbb55c293d99f8ddc211</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T17:46:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-bolsonaro-sons-carlos-and-race-for-power-brazil-south--3d3858e0bb77.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-bolsonaro-sons-carlos-and-race-for-power-brazil-south" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro is not the only member of his family campaigning in his father’s shadow. The former president's eldest son, who is now polling neck and neck with incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, can count on two of his brothers, who are standing in the senatorial and legislative elections. In Santa Catarina, one of Brazil’s most pro-Bolsonaro southern states, their surname alone is enough to secure victory.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>‘National security threat’: Trump’s latest attack on US media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1a1b3b40e1d65e9ed37d43cefe5dfc05125b5824388da90d46804951af5bdc2</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T16:35:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-national-security-threat-trump-s-latest-attack-on-us-media--f4e45c3c4ab7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-national-security-threat-trump-s-latest-attack-on-us-media" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Monday accused mainstream media outlets of being a “cancer” and national security threat in his latest attack on members of the press. It comes after Trump barred journalists from CNN, MS NOW and Politico from the White House, with the three media outlets saying Monday they would sue the Trump administration, calling the ban a “blatant violation” of the First Amendment.</summary></entry><entry><title>Typhoon Dujuan: Japan urges two million to evacuate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69c0e9a1c09f5d8d160734cb10c46d841727fe57923aff8aa1a29815a1a114cd</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T16:12:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-typhoon-dujuan-japan-urges-two-million-to-evacuate--18e5b026addc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-typhoon-dujuan-japan-urges-two-million-to-evacuate" /><summary type="html">Japan’s Meteorological Agency has warned of an "imminent threat to life" as Typhoon Dujuan bears down on the country, with nearly two million people urged to evacuate across six prefectures, including Tokyo.</summary></entry><entry><title>French singer Amanda Lear accuses US star Miley Cyrus of 'copying' 1970s hit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3fa415403aba7d0fc551460bc7cbe920abce4344ec78dbec824f4bcdcb6972e</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T16:08:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-singer-amanda-lear-accuses-us-star-miley-cyrus-copying-1970s-hit--81607468a96a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-singer-amanda-lear-accuses-us-star-miley-cyrus-copying-1970s-hit" /><summary type="html">French disco diva Amanda Lear accused Miley Cyrus on Monday of plagiarising her 1970s song "The Sphinx" in the US pop star's new track, "Redlights". However, Lear later added that she was not interested in a lawsuit.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Bayeux Tapestry craze prompts photo ban at British Museum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe646187633e8a9e5fc949eabb45b2b1ed2cc2b86a9c2655e720ee76cac73624</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:11:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T15:45:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-bayeux-tapestry-craze-prompts-photo-ban-at-british-museum--545565e72784.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-bayeux-tapestry-craze-prompts-photo-ban-at-british-museum" /><summary type="html">The British Museum said on Monday that it has banned people from taking photos of the Bayeux Tapestry to prevent crowds from backing up at the new exhibit. The 1,000-year-old artwork is on display in the UK after an unprecedented loan from France, and tickets are sold out until December 31.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU fines Google €403 million for improperly using location data</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60f6c04bae48449afa60f2b6da7c11396287f09b200c0aee55bcbdce46df9124</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T15:05:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-eu-fines-google-_403-million-for-improperly-using-location-data--76f449cd2c22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-eu-fines-google-%E2%82%AC403-million-for-improperly-using-location-data" /><summary type="html">Ireland, on behalf of the European Union, said Monday it had fined Google €403 million for improperly using users' location data between May 2018 and February 2020. However, the eight-year delay drew some criticism, as the European Consumer Organisation said that "can be as harmful as no enforcement at all".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Merz’s election setback: What it means for Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae98e92c5380b2bd428b3834f4e3306120fa0708646d9a97eeb51584a19a96af</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T15:02:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/merz-s-election-setback-what-it-means-for-germany--455ac69abf37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/merz-s-election-setback-what-it-means-for-germany" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and CDU representatives held a press conference on Monday, September 21, after the party suffered its worst regional election defeat in postwar Germany. Merz called the result in Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania a “disaster”, as the CDU fell below the 5% threshold for entering the state parliament. Helmut Schmidt fellow at the German Marshall Fund of the US, Markus Ziener, shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>France and Canada deepen economic and defense ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f81a47ad680ebdc55bbd25cbf665bbef12504f97dccc45cb74d64cda7bb51ad</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:59:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-and-canada-deepen-economic-and-defense-ties--512757cad0d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-and-canada-deepen-economic-and-defense-ties" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney have announced plans to deepen economic ties between their countries following a meeting at the weekend. Macron welcomed Carney in Saint-Pierre-et-Miquelon, a French territory off the coast of Canada’s Newfoundland. The two leaders discussed opportunities to share infrastructure in the space and defence sectors, as Canada’s trade relationship with the US deteriorates and Europe looks to diversify its energy supplies. Bryan Quinn has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia left without US help against Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfce7bd38c7bce6babd21dafe500ce62848aed7655a2ee9cd4133c75d9193e3e</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:57:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-left-without-us-help-against-houthis--69e955589d82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-left-without-us-help-against-houthis" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia is weighing Washington’s refusal to help fend off Houthi attacks after Riyadh requested US assistance, despite the two countries being longstanding allies and President Donald Trump and his family maintaining close personal ties with Saudi leaders. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details on this alliance.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK: Fallout over Charles Spencer’s Diana Memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75931f77a339383ba2154f31b0e3ba78c967aad8b2d8e8ee868cb089e83a8878</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:41:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uk-fallout-over-charles-spencer-s-diana-memoir--3ef3c2b52f8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uk-fallout-over-charles-spencer-s-diana-memoir" /><summary type="html">In the UK, fallout continues over the explosive memoirs of Princess Diana’s brother. Charles Spencer on Sunday accused King Charles of “gaslighting” him over his account of events surrounding Diana’s death, detailed in a book due to be released on Tuesday. Earl Spencer claims the monarch was “giddily elated” in the immediate aftermath of her death. Carys Garland has the story.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Government hosts energy meeting amid fuel price tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a94e4886fce44f948dc187fe2d47e96a21df2edf5fe3bb1338c320bd8bc2f457</id><updated>2026-09-22T05:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:39:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-government-hosts-energy-meeting-amid-fuel-price-tensions--84ccdd839cba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-government-hosts-energy-meeting-amid-fuel-price-tensions" /><summary type="html">The French government is holding urgent meetings today as it looks for ways to tackle rapidly rising fuel prices. Drivers are paying record-high prices for diesel, as the war in Iran disrupts crude oil shipments from the Middle East. But with public discontent growing, the government has limited options, as France’s finances are already under pressure. This report is from Bryan Quinn and our colleagues at France Télévisions.</summary></entry></feed>
